From fd7c120fca969737d9a87fdedcfae6bc268b7204 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Devin Moore <devinmoore@google.com>
Date: Fri, 12 Jun 2026 16:10:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Reapply "Handle corrupted read/write pointers in read
 funcitons"

This reverts commit 11165074cdd90594e1935ee2b9edceb822a2957f.

Fixed beginRead() check to only apply to kSynchronizedReadWrite flavors.
The other unsync flavor is expected to have overflows when the readers
are too slow to keep with the writer.

Also added tests for beginRead() specifically and tests for the unsync
overflow behavior.

Test: atest fmq_unit_tests
Bug: 504768739
Bug: 514861024
Flag: EXEMPT BUGFIX
